{"title":"How a hash table finds a home for every key","sub":"Hash the key, take the remainder, and that is the bucket. Collisions share a bucket in a short chain.","kind":"grid","interval":1150,"grid":{"rowLabels":["bucket 0","bucket 1","bucket 2","bucket 3","bucket 4","bucket 5","bucket 6","bucket 7"]},"legend":[["a","key just stored"],["b","checked during lookup"],["good","found"]],"frames":[{"caption":"8 empty buckets. A key's bucket is <b>hash(key) mod 8</b>. Here the toy hash adds up letter positions: a = 1, b = 2, ...","cells":[[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null]],"cellCls":{},"stats":[["Keys",0],["Load factor","0.00"]]},{"caption":"hash(<b>cat</b>) = 24, and 24 mod 8 = <b>0</b>. Bucket 0 is empty: store it there in one step.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null]],"cellCls":{"0,0":"a"},"stats":[["Keys",1],["Load factor","0.12"]]},{"caption":"hash(<b>dog</b>) = 26, and 26 mod 8 = <b>2</b>. Bucket 2 is empty: store it there in one step.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog",null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null]],"cellCls":{"2,0":"a"},"stats":[["Keys",2],["Load factor","0.25"]]},{"caption":"hash(<b>bee</b>) = 12, and 12 mod 8 = <b>4</b>. Bucket 4 is empty: store it there in one step.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog",null,null],[null,null,null],["bee",null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null]],"cellCls":{"4,0":"a"},"stats":[["Keys",3],["Load factor","0.38"]]},{"caption":"hash(<b>owl</b>) = 50, and 50 mod 8 = <b>2</b>. Bucket 2 already holds dog: a <b>collision</b>. Chain it on the end.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog","owl",null],[null,null,null],["bee",null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null]],"cellCls":{"2,1":"a"},"stats":[["Keys",4],["Load factor","0.50"]]},{"caption":"hash(<b>ant</b>) = 35, and 35 mod 8 = <b>3</b>. Bucket 3 is empty: store it there in one step.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog","owl",null],["ant",null,null],["bee",null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null]],"cellCls":{"3,0":"a"},"stats":[["Keys",5],["Load factor","0.62"]]},{"caption":"hash(<b>fox</b>) = 45, and 45 mod 8 = <b>5</b>. Bucket 5 is empty: store it there in one step.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog","owl",null],["ant",null,null],["bee",null,null],["fox",null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null]],"cellCls":{"5,0":"a"},"stats":[["Keys",6],["Load factor","0.75"]]},{"caption":"hash(<b>emu</b>) = 39, and 39 mod 8 = <b>7</b>. Bucket 7 is empty: store it there in one step.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog","owl",null],["ant",null,null],["bee",null,null],["fox",null,null],[null,null,null],["emu",null,null]],"cellCls":{"7,0":"a"},"stats":[["Keys",7],["Load factor","0.88"]]},{"caption":"hash(<b>yak</b>) = 37, and 37 mod 8 = <b>5</b>. Bucket 5 already holds fox: a <b>collision</b>. Chain it on the end.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog","owl",null],["ant",null,null],["bee",null,null],["fox","yak",null],[null,null,null],["emu",null,null]],"cellCls":{"5,1":"a"},"stats":[["Keys",8],["Load factor","1.00"]]},{"caption":"Look up <b>owl</b>: hash it again, 50 mod 8 = 2. Jump straight to bucket 2, no searching the others.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog","owl",null],["ant",null,null],["bee",null,null],["fox","yak",null],[null,null,null],["emu",null,null]],"cellCls":{"2,0":"b"},"stats":[["Keys",8],["Load factor","1.00"]]},{"caption":"Bucket 2 holds dog first: not it. Check the next one in the chain.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog","owl",null],["ant",null,null],["bee",null,null],["fox","yak",null],[null,null,null],["emu",null,null]],"cellCls":{"2,0":"b","2,1":"b"},"stats":[["Keys",8],["Load factor","1.00"]]},{"caption":"Found <b>owl</b> after 2 checks. With a good hash and few keys per bucket, lookups take a constant number of checks: <b>O(1) expected</b>.","cells":[["cat",null,null],[null,null,null],["dog","owl",null],["ant",null,null],["bee",null,null],["fox","yak",null],[null,null,null],["emu",null,null]],"cellCls":{"2,1":"good"},"stats":[["Keys",8],["Load factor","1.00"]]}]}